REVISION 2 EXACT-BYTES REVIEW — RETURN, NOT ACK.

Artifact reviewed:
  path    docs/plans/2026-09-01-recall-construction-prd.md
  bytes   36095
  sha256  b69819b85fd03955505a5a836b50d2560392d00447f97b59d27b87da6f75a618

The file matches the published bytes. V1-V4 are materially repaired, and the R11.7 correction now states the measured shipped-output defect rather than hiding it. I also accept the external review's central disposition: this can become the integrity spine of recall construction, but these bytes are not yet a complete product/scientific PRD.

FOUR LOAD-BEARING BLOCKERS REMAIN.

1. R7'S NEW 2x2 COURT CONTRADICTS R2.

The two refusal oracles are:
- (PA,IY) refuses because two predicates cannot bind inside one cell that asserts a single claim.
- (PB,IX) refuses because a predicate cannot cross a cell boundary.

Neither follows from this document's own architecture. R2 separates contiguous computational cells from semantic/evidentiary supports; R9 already says claims and cells have different identities. A cell may carry several claims, and a claim may overlap or cross cells. Refusing those two combinations silently reinstates cell == claim and makes the many-to-many incidence relation impossible.

This is not an editorial objection: the new "falsifiable" court would force an implementation to violate the scientific separation it is meant to protect.

Required repair:
- state explicitly that cells are carriers, not semantic atoms;
- make cell-to-artifact incidence many-to-many;
- allow overlapping/discontinuous/cross-cell claims without duplication or truncation;
- define compatibility laws over admitted plan membership, eligible-region support, surviving relation endpoints, repair/retraction consistency, and loss-recording in the fixed-view projection;
- replace PA/PB x IX/IY with fixtures that violate one of those actual laws. Merely changing clause count is not incompatibility evidence.

This is the strongest point in the external review's proposed "cells are not claims" requirement, and I support it.

2. V6 STILL LAUNDERS FOUR COORDINATES INTO ONE ENUM.

R10.1 gives:
  BaselineHeuristic | ProviderResolved | Adjudicated | AuthorityAbsent

Those cases are not alternatives on one axis. They mix construction route, resolver outcome, authenticity/authority availability, and (via R8.6) estimand conditioning. Lawful states already require combinations the enum cannot represent:

- provider-resolved but authenticity unverified;
- authentically provider-produced but uncalibrated or scientifically inadmissible;
- human-adjudicated yet segmentation-conditioned for a named quantity;
- baseline recipe known, but no scientific admission;
- route unknown while structural conformance still passes.

There is also an internal contradiction. R3.3 correctly says missing authority does not establish heuristic construction. Yet Court R10 derives BaselineHeuristic from "an artifact built through RecallSegmenter" without specifying a route/recipe witness, while RecallSegmenter.segment currently returns only RecallGraph[Checked]. The graph bytes cannot prove which route produced them. Likewise, conformance from the resolver cannot by itself justify ProviderResolved as an authority class; R3-FORGED exists precisely because caller-invented provider bytes can be perfectly conformant.

Required repair: independently represent and derive, at minimum:
- construction route/basis, bound to executing recipe/code/config and subject;
- authority/authenticity verification under a named trust root;
- calibration and use-specific scientific admission;
- per-estimand conditioning classification: invariant under a named transformation witness, segmentation/interpretation-conditioned, or no lawful cross-construction scalar.

The last item is what R8.6 actually needs. It cannot be replaced by a construction-global route label. Benchmark calibration must remain another independent fact: current BenchReport can render CALIBRATED from frozen-set/protocol checks while BenchCase and CaseRun carry no recall-construction standing. A heuristic recall must not acquire an unqualified sole "CALIBRATED" presentation.

Courts must include direct-segmenter recipe witness, caller-label refusal, subject/receipt swap refusal, recipe/config mutation changing construction identity, legacy decode no-upgrade, authentic-but-inadmissible, and the existing consumer render paths. Do not "mutate the qualification" directly as the current court says; mutate its admitted basis and require recomputation.

3. THE CENTRAL ARTIFACT AND USABLE VERTICAL SLICE ARE ABSENT.

Section C lists contract families but does not say what a build returns when resolution is partial, what is serialized, what owns alternatives, what is compared across constructions, or what exact admitted object projects to RecallGraph[Checked]. Section A names downstream consumers but no milestone delivers an end-to-end path into them.

I agree with the external review on the obligation, not with adopting its illustrative Scala names by fiat. The revision should specify responsibilities and boundaries without pre-deciding public vocabulary:
- observation plus derivation identity;
- coordinate dialect and eligible regions;
- admitted cell plan;
- interpretation artifacts and unresolved alternatives;
- many-to-many incidence and compatibility witness;
- authority/conformance/admission witnesses;
- complete construction identity;
- a family/search receipt when alternatives remain;
- a named fixed-view projection into the existing aligner;
- downstream results bound to the construction identity and independent qualification coordinates.

The first usable slice must be explicit:
  transcript -> witnessed baseline construction -> qualified fixed RecallGraph view -> existing GraphHsmm/signature path -> result/rendering that preserves construction standing.

If the author does not want to add that product layer here, rename/recast these bytes as the integrity/design contract and create a separate short product PRD. Calling the present document the complete PRD is not supportable.

4. V5 STILL OVERSTATES COURT EXECUTABILITY.

R11 is headed "court EXECUTABLE" while its acceptance oracle requires a canonical projection and complete-construction identity that do not exist, and the same section says the failure type and acquire/document boundary remain unsettled. What is executable today is the red defect probe; the full acceptance court is design-stage. R4's calibrated cells likewise lack the frozen observation model/target/prior/decision fixture and are blocked on Q-A2/P2. R10's court depends on the missing artifact and coordinates above.

Use a truthful registry/status:
  court id | frozen fixture/mutation | dependency | machine oracle | required disposition/equalities | current status

Distinguish "red probe executable now", "acceptance court design-stage", "blocked on model/gold", and "empirical gate". A named paragraph is not an executable court.

DISPOSITION OF THE REST OF THE EXTERNAL REVIEW.

Adopt into the contract:
- a provider call is one joint observation, not necessarily a point set;
- call-wide coordinate error must be modeled separately from residual per-boundary jitter;
- calibration target is declared and may be an exact plan, acceptable-plan set, region/distribution, or task loss;
- a named reversible decision view may be derived from uncertainty, but must retain posterior/alternatives/loss/rule and never masquerade as resolved truth;
- claim-first semantics and compatibility laws;
- an early end-to-end vertical slice.

Route separately rather than silently deciding here:
- exact public Scala names and module placement;
- complete Checked -> StructurallyChecked rename (N5 should say "not required here; any rename must be complete/versioned", not "out of scope at any size");
- raw-audio/transcript-derivation identity expansion;
- the two-level ClaimId/ClaimAssertion identity choice (R12 ADR);
- P2 ownership/REB/budget (owner/chief governance gate).

ACK CONDITIONS FOR THE NEXT EXACT ARTIFACT:
A. R7 no longer equates cells with claims.
B. R10 is factored into non-implicative, derived coordinates and its courts cannot be satisfied by caller labels.
C. The artifact is either truthfully an integrity design contract plus a routed product PRD, or contains the central artifact, projection, and vertical slice itself.
D. Court status is mechanically honest.
E. Fresh byte count/hash; zero carried ACKs.

No implementation, ADR decision, public vocabulary, module, dependency, bead, path, reservation, or authority claimed.
